Modern GPT Models

Interestingly, GPT models don't use fixed sine/cosine encodings anymore.

Instead they use:

Learned Position Embeddings

or

RoPE (Rotary Positional Embeddings)

Used in:

Llama
DeepSeek
Qwen
Why RoPE is Better

Suppose:

Training:

Kubernetes manages pods

Later:

Kubernetes efficiently manages pods

RoPE helps preserve relative positions:

Kubernetes → manages

even if more words are inserted.

This improves long-context understanding.

